      }
    },
    "Binding used" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "所用结合数据"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "所用結合數據"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Binds to the benzodiazepine site at the interface of α and γ subunits on GABA-A receptors, acting as a positive allosteric modulator. Enhances the effect of GABA by increasing the frequency of chloride channel opening, leading to neuronal hyperpolarization and reduced excitability. Produces anxiolytic, sedative, hypnotic, anticonvulsant, and muscle relaxant effects." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "结合于 GABA-A 受体上 α 和 γ 亚单位界面的苯二氮䓬位点,作为正向变构调节剂。通过增加氯离子通道开放频率增强 GABA 的效应,导致神经元超极化和兴奋性降低。产生抗焦虑、镇静、催眠、抗惊厥和肌肉松弛效应。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "結合於 GABA-A 受體上 α 和 γ 亞單位界面的苯二氮䓬位點,作為正向變構調節劑。透過增加氯離子通道開放頻率增強 GABA 的效應,導致神經元超極化和興奮性降低。產生抗焦慮、鎮靜、催眠、抗驚厥和肌肉鬆弛效應。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Binds to the α2δ-1 subunit of voltage-gated calcium channels (VGCCs), reducing calcium influx at presynaptic nerve terminals. This decreases the release of excitatory neurotransmitters including glutamate, norepinephrine, substance P, and calcitonin gene-related peptide. Despite the name, gabapentinoids do not interact with GABA receptors or GABA metabolism." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "结合于电压门控钙通道 (VGCC) 的 α2δ-1 亚单位,减少突触前神经末梢的钙内流。这减少兴奋性神经递质(包括谷氨酸、去甲肾上腺素、P 物质和降钙素基因相关肽)的释放。尽管名字如此,加巴喷丁类药物并不与 GABA 受体或 GABA 代谢相互作用。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "結合於電壓門控鈣通道 (VGCC) 的 α2δ-1 亞單位,減少突觸前神經末梢的鈣內流。這減少興奮性神經傳導物質(包括麩胺酸、去甲腎上腺素、P 物質和降鈣素基因相關肽)的釋放。儘管名字如此,加巴噴丁類藥物並不與 GABA 受體或 GABA 代謝相互作用。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "bioavailability" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "生物利用度"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "生物利用度"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bioavailability" : {

    },
    "Bioavailability (F)" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "生物利用度 (F)"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "生物利用度 (F)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bioavailability versus dose: gabapentin falls as the dose rises, pregabalin stays flat." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "生物利用度随剂量的变化：加巴喷丁随剂量升高而下降，普瑞巴林保持平稳。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "生物利用度隨劑量的變化：加巴噴丁隨劑量升高而下降，普瑞巴林保持平穩。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Biweekly" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "两周一次"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "兩週一次"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bliss" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "极乐"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "極樂"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks 5-HT₂A while weakly inhibiting serotonin reuptake. The receptor block dominates at low doses, which is why trazodone reached far more people as a sleep drug than as an antidepressant." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断5-HT₂A，同时弱抑制5-羟色胺再摄取。低剂量时受体阻断占主导，这就是曲唑酮作为助眠药比作为抗抑郁药触及了多得多的人的原因。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷5-HT₂A，同時弱抑制血清素回收。低劑量時受體阻斷佔主導，這就是曲唑酮作為助眠藥比作為抗憂鬱藥觸及了多得多的人的原因。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks dopamine D2 receptors in the mesolimbic pathway, reducing positive psychotic symptoms. Whether this compound also carries the 5-HT2A antagonism that distinguishes the second-generation agents, and the histamine, muscarinic and adrenergic activity that drives sedation and orthostasis, varies across the class and is not characterized here." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断中脑边缘通路的多巴胺 D2 受体，减轻精神病性阳性症状。该化合物是否同时具有区分第二代药物的 5-HT2A 拮抗作用，以及导致镇静与体位性低血压的组胺、毒蕈碱与肾上腺素能活性，在同类药物中各不相同，此处未作说明。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷中腦邊緣通路的多巴胺 D2 受體，減輕精神病性陽性症狀。該化合物是否同時具有區分第二代藥物的 5-HT2A 拮抗作用，以及導致鎮靜與姿勢性低血壓的組織胺、蕈毒鹼與腎上腺素能活性，在同類藥物中各不相同，此處未作說明。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks histamine H1 receptors, reducing the itching, flare, wheal and vasodilation of the histamine response. Whether this compound crosses into the central nervous system — the difference between a sedating first-generation antihistamine with a muscarinic load and a peripherally selective second-generation one — is not characterized here." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断组胺 H1 受体，减轻组胺反应中的瘙痒、红晕、风团与血管扩张。该化合物是否进入中枢神经系统——这正是具有毒蕈碱负荷、会引起嗜睡的第一代抗组胺药与外周选择性的第二代抗组胺药之间的区别——此处未作说明。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷組織胺 H1 受體，減輕組織胺反應中的搔癢、紅暈、風疹塊與血管擴張。該化合物是否進入中樞神經系統——這正是具有蕈毒鹼負荷、會引起嗜睡的第一代抗組織胺藥與周邊選擇性的第二代抗組織胺藥之間的區別——此處未作說明。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks N-methyl-D-aspartate (NMDA) glutamate receptors, typically by binding within the ion channel pore as a non-competitive antagonist. NMDA receptor blockade reduces excitatory glutamatergic neurotransmission, producing dissociative anesthesia, analgesia, and altered states of consciousness characterized by feelings of detachment from body and environment." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断 N-甲基-D-天冬氨酸 (NMDA) 谷氨酸受体,通常作为非竞争性拮抗剂结合于离子通道孔内。NMDA 受体阻断减少兴奋性谷氨酸能神经传递,产生解离性麻醉、镇痛和以与身体和环境脱离感为特征的意识改变状态。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷 N-甲基-D-天門冬胺酸 (NMDA) 麩胺酸受體,通常作為非競爭性拮抗劑結合於離子通道孔內。NMDA 受體阻斷減少興奮性麩胺酸能神經傳導,產生解離性麻醉、鎮痛和以與身體和環境脫離感為特徵的意識改變狀態。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks noradrenaline and dopamine reuptake, leaving serotonin alone — the activating end of the family." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断去甲肾上腺素和多巴胺的再摄取，不动5-羟色胺——这一类里偏兴奋的一端。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷正腎上腺素和多巴胺的回收，不動血清素——這一類裡偏興奮的一端。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks serotonin and noradrenaline reuptake like an SNRI, and also histamine, muscarinic and α₁ receptors. That extra binding is the sedation, the dry mouth, and the narrow margin in overdose." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "像SNRI一样阻断5-羟色胺和去甲肾上腺素的再摄取，同时还结合组胺、毒蕈碱和α₁受体。多出来的这部分结合，就是镇静、口干，以及过量时安全窗口狭窄的来源。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "像SNRI一樣阻斷血清素和正腎上腺素的回收，同時還結合組織胺、蕈毒鹼和α₁受體。多出來的這部分結合，就是鎮靜、口乾，以及過量時安全窗口狹窄的來源。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks serotonin and noradrenaline reuptake together. The noradrenaline share grows with dose, so a low dose can behave much like an SSRI." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "同时阻断5-羟色胺和去甲肾上腺素的再摄取。去甲肾上腺素那一份随剂量增大，因此低剂量时表现可以很像SSRI。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "同時阻斷血清素和正腎上腺素的回收。正腎上腺素那一份隨劑量增大，因此低劑量時表現可以很像SSRI。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks serotonin reuptake and acts on several serotonin receptors directly, agonist at some and antagonist at others. The receptor work is what separates it from an SSRI, not the transporter block they share." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "既阻断5-羟色胺再摄取，又直接作用于多个5-羟色胺受体，对一些是激动，对另一些是拮抗。把它和SSRI区分开的是受体上的这部分作用，而不是两者共有的转运体阻断。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "既阻斷血清素回收，又直接作用於多個血清素受體，對一些是激動，對另一些是拮抗。把它和SSRI區分開的是受體上的這部分作用，而不是兩者共有的轉運體阻斷。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks the enzyme that breaks monoamines down, rather than the transporters that recycle them, so all three rise. The tyramine restriction and the long interaction list both follow from that." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断的是分解单胺的酶，而不是回收它们的转运体，所以三种单胺都会升高。酪胺饮食限制和那一长串相互作用，都由此而来。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷的是分解單胺的酶，而不是回收它們的轉運體，所以三種單胺都會升高。酪胺飲食限制和那一長串交互作用，都由此而來。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks the noradrenaline transporter and leaves the other two. In the prefrontal cortex that same transporter is what clears dopamine, so the effect there is not as purely noradrenergic as the name reads." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "只阻断去甲肾上腺素转运体，另外两种不动。在前额叶皮层，清除多巴胺的正是同一个转运体，所以那里的作用并不像名字读起来那样纯粹是去甲肾上腺素性的。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "只阻斷正腎上腺素轉運體，另外兩種不動。在前額葉皮質，清除多巴胺的正是同一個轉運體，所以那裡的作用並不像名字讀起來那樣純粹是正腎上腺素性的。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks the serotonin transporter and little else, which is why its effects and its side effects are both mostly serotonergic." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "几乎只阻断5-羟色胺转运体，因此它的作用与副作用大多都是5-羟色胺性的。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "幾乎只阻斷血清素轉運體，因此它的作用與副作用大多都是血清素性的。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blood pressure" : {
